t upon successful deposit.","params":{"amount":"The amount of the underlying token to stake."}},"eip712Domain()":{"details":"See {IERC-5267}."},"initialize(address,address,address,uint32)":{"custom:revert":"ZeroInitialAuthority If `initialAuthority` is the zero address.ZeroStakeTokenImplementation If `initialImplementation` is the zero address.","details":"This is the initializer for the upgradeable contract. It sets the initial authority for access control, configures EIP-712 for signatures, stores the underlying asset and stake token implementation, sets the global lockup period, and deploys a new ERC1967 proxy for the StakeToken. This function can only be called once on the proxy.","params":{"_underlying":"The ERC20 token that users will deposit to receive stake tokens.","initialAuthority":"The address granted the authority role for access management.","initialImplementation":"The address of the `StakeToken` implementation contract to be used for the proxy.","lockupPeriod":"The global time in seconds that a user's deposit is locked before they can withdraw."}},"isConsumingScheduledOp()":{"details":"Returns true only in the context of a delayed restricted call, at the moment that the scheduled operation is being consumed. Prevents denial of service for delayed restricted calls in the case that the contract performs attacker controlled calls."},"isUnstakeLocked(address)":{"details":"Lock is enforced until the returned timestamp; returns false if no lock is set.","params":{"account":"The account to check."},"returns":{"locked":"True if the account cannot withdraw yet.","unlockAt":"The timestamp when the account can withdraw (0 if no lock)."}},"nonces(address)":{"details":"Returns the next unused nonce for an address."},"proxiableUUID()":{"details":"Implementation of the ERC-1822 {proxiableUUID} function. This returns the storage slot used by the implementation. It is used to validate the implementation's compatibility when performing an upgrade. IMPORTANT: A proxy p